issue (high): 🟠 **Caption text breaks text locators on recorded runs** **(blocking)**

The caption is DOM text, so `getByText('Save')` went from 1 to 2 matches once `__rec.step('WHEN the user clicks "Save"')` ran (Playwright 1.60). The probe's `n !== 1` check then fails a passing spec.

Evidence: `skills/workflow/autonomous-workflow/rules/aw-tester-intent-probe.md:125` (caption set before find())

```js
caption.dataset.label = label || '';
// CSS: [data-r=caption]::after { content: attr(data-label); }
```

_Pseudo-code — verify before applying._

